# Prettier mangles MkDocs admonition syntax — every `!!! note "..."` block
# requires its content to be 4-space-indented, and prettier strips that
# indent. The docs auto-update workflow then re-adds the indent on next
# merge, kicking off an endless lint-vs-docs churn cycle that blocks
# unrelated PRs. user_docs/ is rendered by mkdocs (see mkdocs.yml), not
# by anything that needs prettier's normalization.
user_docs/

# Same problem, different file: prettier's markdown parser reads the
# underscores in our MCP tool names as emphasis delimiters and rewrites them
# — `create_from_template` becomes `create*from_template`, `synthetic_*`
# becomes `synthetic\_\*`. That corrupts the rendered text rather than
# normalising it. CLAUDE.md is also regenerated by the docs automation, so
# every regeneration would re-break the linter on unrelated PRs.
CLAUDE.md

# The semantic engine's parity golden: one result row per line on purpose, so a
# deliberate regeneration diffs row by row. Prettier would put every value on its
# own line.
connect_labs/semantic/tests/fixtures/kmc_rollup_golden.json

# A vendored, already-minified third-party decoder (jsQR, Apache-2.0). Reformatting it would
# turn a 130 KB line into a diff nobody can review.
connect_labs/static/supply_chain/field/jsQR.min.js
